Write a program that prompts the user for a file name and reads the contents of the file. The program should then print the contents of the file to the console.

Here is an example of how you might implement this program:
```
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
    FILE *fp;
    char filename[200];
    char contents[200];

    printf("Enter the name of the file to read: ");
    fgets(filename, sizeof(filename), stdin);

    fp = fopen(filename, "r");
    if (fp == NULL) {
        printf("Error: Could not open file %s\n", filename);
        return 1;
    }

    fseek(fp, 0, SEEK_END);
    long length = ftell(fp);
    fseek(fp, 0, SEEK_SET);

    fread(contents, sizeof(char), length, fp);

    printf("Contents of file: %s\n", contents);

    fclose(fp);

    return 0;
}
```
This program prompts the user to enter the name of the file to read, reads the contents of the file, and prints the contents to the console.

